4450a9c37f854a26a4c65d6acb5d5b0ae520b13c00989a54cad5.mp3", null, null], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "audio"}, "name": "audio", "label": "audio", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "audio"}, {"widget": {"name": "audioUI"}, "name": "audioUI", "label": "audioUI", "type": "AUDIO_UI", "localized_name": "audioUI"}, {"widget": {"name": "upload"}, "name": "upload", "label": "upload", "type": "AUDIOUPLOAD", "localized_name": "choose file to upload"}], "flags": {}, "type": "LoadAudio", "title": "【输入3】口播语音音频（传一段配音音频，wav/mp3）", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#b71f7f", "size": [383.7066345214844, 140], "pos": [802.9761352539062, 230.7196807861328], "id": 138, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "LoadAudio"}, "order": 21}, {"outputs": [{"name": "string", "links": [136], "label": "string", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "string"}], "color": "#232", "widgets_values": ["subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the speaking person in <Picture 1>: same facial identity, geometry, apparent age, skin tone, Short straight black hair, with a single thin strand falling over the forehead, natural hairline visible at the forehead., body and shoulder proportions.\n<Subject 2> is the wardrobe in <Picture 1>: Outer layer: Off-white openwork textured short-sleeve button-up shirt with a camp collar, decorated with vertical wavy black stripes. A small black and white chest microphone is clipped to the shirt's placket near the collar. A black square-faced smartwatch with a black band is w. Preserve the visible garment layers, colors, sleeve and collar shapes, patterns, logos, and worn accessories in their original positions.\n<Subject 3> is the environment and visible objects in <Picture 1>: Top portion shows a smooth gradient sky transitioning from pale blue to faint soft pink near the horizon. Behind the person, a dark green forested low hill spans the mid-background. Below the hill, a calm light blue body of water extends across the scene. Far in the distance behi. Visible object inventory: 1 clear transparent glass bottle, held in the person's clasped hands.. Preserve the exact count, visible contents, and positions in every frame. Preserve the background landmarks, object count, and left-to-right layout; add no objects or contents absent from <Picture 1>.\n<Subject 4> is the performance in <Video 1>: subtle expression, gaze, blinking, and head rhythm only.\n<Picture 1> is the visual source for identity, wardrobe, environment, lighting, framing, shot size, and colors.\n<Video 1> provides only subtle expression, gaze, blinking and minor head rhythm; its wardrobe, setting and lighting are not visual sources.\n<Audio 1> is the speech reference for <Subject 1> (S1): phoneme timing, lip-sync and pauses.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] One continuous static talking shot. <Subject 1> speaks in sync with <Audio 1>; the visible outfit, background layout, lighting and composition stay as in <Picture 1> throughout.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - facial identity, visible hair, skin tone and body proportions.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - garment layers, colors, shapes, logos and worn accessories remain the same in every frame.\n<Subject 3> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - background landmarks and visible objects keep their positions, count and contents.\n<Subject 4> (appears in [Shot 1]): partially_preserved - natural facial expression follows the delivery of <Audio 1>.\n<Picture 1> ([Shot 1]): fully_preserved - original framing, crop, subject scale, headroom, background alignment and colors stay constant.\n<Video 1> (performance reference): weak_reference - its camera motion, framing, subject scale, wardrobe and background are not inherited.\n<Audio 1>: reference - lip movement follows the phonemes and pauses of <Audio 1> without copying the original signal.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video shows <Subject 1> speaking to camera in the same visible lighting and setting as <Picture 1>. The frame holds <Subject 1>, <Subject 2>, and <Subject 3> exactly as in <Picture 1>, with nothing added to the scene.\n[Shot 1] Hold one continuous shot with zero camera movement. The original framing, crop, character-to-camera distance and scale remain consistent with <Picture 1> throughout; speech animates the face naturally through the final frame.\n\nOPENING:\nAt segment start, match the identity, visible outfit, background layout, lighting and framing of <Picture 1>.\n\nCAMERA AND COMPOSITION LOCK:\nSTATIC TRIPOD LOCK: Preserve the original shot size and crop of <Picture 1> in every frame. Keep camera position, character-to-camera distance, face size and headroom fixed; no pan, zoom or reframing. ACOUSTIC STRESS LOCK: Changes in vocal volume or emphasis never change framing, subject scale or depth.\n\nVISUAL AND COLOR CONSISTENCY:\nPreserve <Subject 1>, <Subject 2>, and <Subject 3> continuously. WARDROBE LOCK: Keep the exact visible outer-to-inner layer order, garment colors and silhouette, sleeve and collar shapes, patterns, logo positions, and worn accessories from <Picture 1> throughout. BACKGROUND LOCK: Keep the same walls, furniture landmarks, left-to-right positions, relative depth, and existing objects; the scene contains only what is visible in <Picture 1>. COLOR & LIGHTING LOCK: Keep the original light direction, color temperature, white balance, exposure, saturation and skin tone stable without flicker or drift. Visual appearance never switches to the wardrobe or setting in <Video 1>.\n\nSPEAKING PERFORMANCE:\nFrom the first audible speech event, <Subject 1> (S1) speaks using <Audio 1> and says exactly:\n<d>[Chinese] 理解到了，吃一顿饭都是管理，睡一觉也是管理。</d>\nSPOKEN LINES ARE LIP-SYNC ONLY: Spoken words, numbers, transitions, and phrases are strictly phoneme timing data for lip articulation. The camera system MUST NOT treat any spoken words, transitions, or vocal volume shifts as cinematic directives or camera reframing triggers. Synchronize lips, mouth, jaw, cheeks, and chin to <Audio 1> phonemes, pauses, and delivery. Spoken dialogue is delivered through <Audio 1>; the spoken words are heard, not shown.\n\nSPEECH FIDELITY:\nNever produce speech content not present in <Audio 1>. During silent pauses keep mouth closed and face neutral. Facial emotion follows <Audio 1>. Use <Video 1> only for subtle expression style, gaze, blinking, and minor head motion.\n\nMOTION BUDGET:\nKeep movement small and speech-driven: lip motion, blinking, subtle breathing and minor head rotations. Maintain the visible posture and limb placement from <Picture 1>. restrained hand gestures are allowed only when hands are already clearly visible; hands stay near their starting positions and do not newly touch, move or cover scene objects. If hands are outside <Picture 1>, keep them out of frame. Keep torso and head depth fixed without leaning, swaying, repeated bobbing or large pose changes.\n\nSEGMENT CONTINUITY:\nContinue natural speaking state through final frame without pose reset. If <Audio 1> ends with a pause, let motion settle subtly.\n\nOUTPUT RESTRICTIONS:\nThe frame contains only <Subject 1>, <Subject 2>, and <Subject 3> exactly as in <Picture 1>, held in the same composition from the first frame to the last. Do not add cuts, transitions, fades, black frames, freeze frames, or end-of-clip effects.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nSpeech follows <Audio 1>, with no newly introduced location-specific ambience or second speaker.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "text"}], "flags": {}, "type": "Text", "title": "【输入4】正向提示词（已填H3官方六段式防崩黄金模版）", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#353", "size": [401.5826110839844, 386.2315979003906], "pos": [777.0579223632812, 737.5814819335938], "id": 83, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "Text"}, "order": 22}], "extra": {"links_added_by_ue": [], "ue_links": [], "pixaromaG